<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05GC">Remark <span data-tag="05GC">10.1.3.9</span>.</a> In the formulation of Definition <a data-tag="05G7" href="/tag/05G7">10.1.3.4</a>, we allow $n$ to be an arbitrary integer. However, for $n &lt; 0$, the notion becomes degenerate: a simplicial object $X_{\bullet }$ is $n$-skeletal if and only if each $X_{m}$ is an initial object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. In this case, $X_{\bullet }$ is an initial object in the $\infty $-category of simplicial objects $\operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{{\bf \Delta }})^{\operatorname{op}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$. </p>
